+      "namespace": "probability.randomtrees",
+      "logical_name": "critical-beta-splitting-finite-drawn-length-recursion-check",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "Finite checks for drawn-length and height bounds",
+      "statement": "The local check_p0340.py run checked 6918 ordered full binary trees through ten leaves with no tree-identity or depth-bound failures. A float64 height-distribution recursion agrees with weighted tree enumeration through n=10 and gives E l(T_128)/128=4.496140445692661. At n=128 the earlier proof's height upper bound is 587.772776 and the tightened upper bound is 205.700923, a 65.00% reduction in that bound. These are finite numerical checks, not a proof of the limiting constant. Current Lean setup was refused by the compute governor; no new Lean verification is claimed.",
+      "proof_text": null,
