+    {
+      "key": "p0013-defects",
+      "namespace": "probability.randomgraphs",
+      "logical_name": "complement-invariant-lovasz-theta-two-defect-reduction",
+      "kind": "lemma",
+      "title": "Two nonnegative defects in expected Lovasz theta",
+      "statement": "For a complement-invariant random graph G on n>=1 vertices, let X=theta(G)/sqrt(n), Y=theta(complement G)/sqrt(n), R=sqrt(XY), and Z=(log X-log Y)/2. Using theta(G)theta(complement G)>=n, E theta(G)/sqrt(n)-1=E(R-1)+E[R(cosh Z-1)], with both terms nonnegative. Therefore the expectation asymptotic at sqrt(n) is equivalent to both defect expectations tending to zero. No defect estimate for G(n,1/2) is proved here. Independent audit pending.",
+      "proof_text": "Assume a graph G on n vertices has complement-invariant law, and write X=theta(G)/sqrt(n), Y=theta(complement G)/sqrt(n). The standard theta-product inequality gives XY>=1. Put R=sqrt(XY) and Z=(log X-log Y)/2. Then X=R exp(Z), Y=R exp(-Z), and complement symmetry gives\n\nE theta(G)/sqrt(n)-1 = E(R-1)+E[R(cosh(Z)-1)].\n\nBoth terms on the right are nonnegative. Therefore the desired expectation asymptotic is equivalent to both defect expectations tending to zero. This distinguishes product tightness from complement imbalance; concentration of Z alone does not control R or the exponential tail. Finite n ensures integrability because 1<=theta(G)<=n.\n\nThe equation follows by averaging E X=E Y and using (X+Y)/2=R cosh Z. No estimate that makes either defect vanish for G(n,1/2) is proved here. It continues P0013-A001 and generalizes the exact-product circulant reduction in P0014-A001. It is not a claimed solution of Conjecture 17.",
+      "assumptions": [
+        "The standard Lovasz theta product inequality."
+      ],
+      "domain": "probability theory",
+      "source": {
+        "source_id": "owner-probability-campaign-w343:p0013-defects",
+        "url": "file:///~/brain_workers/w343/P0013_proof.md",
+        "revision": "author-checked-2026-10-10-pending-w347",
+        "license": "owner-own-work (campaign proof or status note)",
