+    {
+      "key": "p0016-literature",
+      "namespace": "probability.randommatrix",
+      "logical_name": "gaussian-phase-retrieval-extreme-submatrix-literature-answer",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "Cached literature answer for the Gaussian worst-subframe problem",
+      "statement": "The cached LITERATURE_P2.md receipt attributes an answer to Yitzchak Shmalo, Extreme least singular values of Gaussian row submatrices and a phase retrieval stability problem, arXiv:2607.06249 (7 July 2026), Theorem 1.1 and Corollary 1.2. For standard real Gaussian (2m-1)-by-m frames it reports omega(A_m)=4^(-m+o_P(m)), equivalently m^(-1)log omega(A_m)->-log 4 in probability. This matches Randomstrasse101 Open Problem 21; the old attempted_unsolved ranking is stale according to that receipt. The primary paper and its full proof were not newly checked here; confirm the citation and normalization before admitting the status correction. This is a literature record, not an original solution.",
