+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "Finite reproduction of worst Gaussian row-subframe scaling",
+      "statement": "With NumPy RNG seed 343, the local check minimizes the smallest singular value over every m-row subset of 64 standard real Gaussian frames for each m=1,...,6: 384 frames and 40,768 minors. At m=6 the median of 4^m omega is 2.5933238602603175. At m=1 the exact omega law is |N(0,1)|. These finite samples check the row-subframe convention and provide numerical evidence only; they do not establish the asymptotic or an exponential limit law.",
